# This CITATION.cff file activates the "Cite this repository" button on GitHub.
# It is a living document: update it each time a new release is published,
# a Zenodo DOI is minted, or a Software Heritage ID (SWHID) is generated.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MindCraft in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MindCraft"
abstract: >
  MindCraft is an open-source academic platform for designing, deploying and
  collecting data from online behavioural experiments (reaction time,
  decision-making, questionnaires, physiological tasks). It provides a no-code
  study builder, participant management, RGPD-compliant data export and an
  open-science workflow for psychology and cognitive science research.

authors:
